// wp_tick_sla_us — the SLA tick period, in MICROSECONDS.
//
// AXVERITY_EXTENT_WRITE_PATH step 2. The write path has exactly one seal
// trigger today: a record that will not fit the active block. That is fine
// while blocks are 16 KiB and fill in ~47 records, and it is not fine at
// 16 MiB, where a block holds ~48,000 records and a slow producer's data sits
// unsealed until the run ends.
//
// So there are two triggers, with complementary duty cycles:
//
//   at full flight   blocks fill faster than the period, block-full dominates,
//                    and the tick mostly finds work already queued — near-free
//   in slow periods  block-full never fires, and the tick is the ONLY thing
//                    that makes data durable
//
// Microseconds, not milliseconds, because that is the unit slab_open takes
// (bridge slablock.rs, `sla_us`) and converting at one end of a boundary is
// how the two drift apart. Default 200000 = 200 ms.
//
// Override: .axverity-store/config/sla_us
fn wp_tick_sla_us(_u: Unit) -> Int {
  wp_cfg_get(Text("sla_us"), Int(200000))
}
